<title>SINGAPORE: Pacific Andes 1st-half net rises 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Pacific Andes 1st-half net rises 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     51.00 vs   40.67</p>
<p>    Total interim dividend * (cts)    1.54 vs    NA</p>
<p>    Group shr (cts)			12.65 vs   12.10</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cts)    11.48 vs   10.85</p>
<p>    Turnover				723.47 vs  574.60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 53.00 vs   41.47</p>
<p>    Tax					 2.00 vs    0.80</p>
<p>Last day books open: October 22, 1996  </p>
<p>Note - Hong Kong-based frozen seafood company Pacific Andes International Holdings Ltd, owned by Hong Kong's Pacific Andes International Holdings, began trading on the Stock Exchange of Singapore on October 4 after an initial public offering of 61.25 million shares in September.</p>
<p>* The company announced two interim dividends: a first of 0.54 cent and a second of 1.00 cent.</p>
<p>- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
